Skip the final "systemctl --user --wait" check in qubes.WaitForSession when
systemctl is not installed.  Native Guix templates use the Shepherd and ship
no systemd, so the unconditional call would fail; guarding it keeps the rest
of the upstream script verbatim (Marek's preferred minimal adaptation).

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux, qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForSession.
Status: should-upstream (Marek's preferred minimal adaptation: guard the
systemctl call rather than carry a full alternate script); intended for
submission to the Qubes project.

diff --git a/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForSession b/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForSession
index 9146b24..f849294 100755
--- a/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForSession
+++ b/qubes-rpc/qubes.WaitForSession
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ if test "$(qubesdb-read --default=True /qubes-gui-enabled)" = "True"; then
     done
 fi
 
-systemctl --user --wait --quiet is-system-running
+if command -v systemctl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    systemctl --user --wait --quiet is-system-running
+fi
 
 exit 0
